From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:28:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Send the webhook from an outbox

The webhook of 0018 goes in maago.AfterCommit: after the commit, before
the response, three tries in 10 seconds. A webhook down for longer, or
a process that stops in between, and the post is never announced. An
outbox keeps the notice in the database until it has gone. Not written
by hand: copy the app maago has:

    maago add outbox
    maago makemigrations --name outbox

It writes outbox/: a model Job (table outbox_job), the queries that take
a job and put it off, and the worker, with its tests. What it writes is
the project's own now. maago gen refuses until main gives the admin
outbox.Admin, as it did for auth.Admin: a job whose last attempt failed
stays, and shows there with its error. Set its Attempts to 0 to send it
again.

- moveTo writes the job in the request's transaction, where it
  publishes the post:

      outbox.Enqueue(ctx, tx, postPublished, map[string]any{"id": p.ID, "key": p.Key, "title": p.Title, "path": PostDetailURL(p.ID)})

  postPublished is the job's Kind, "post_published". A rollback takes
  the job with it, as AfterCommit dropped its call.
  The payload is the webhook's body as it is. It has the post's key
  now (0039), the address a receiver reads it by from the API; null for
  a post with none. With no webhook URL, there is no job
- main runs the worker beside the server, as package outbox's doc has
  it: outbox.Run(work, db, board.Deliver). Once Serve has stopped, the
  worker takes no more jobs and finishes the one in hand
- Deliver posts one job's payload, once, within notifyWithin, with the
  job's id as the Idempotency-Key header. The outbox tries a job again
  that is not delivered: it waits 2 seconds, then twice as long each
  time, 12 attempts in all. A job goes at least once, not exactly once:
  the same key on a repeat lets the webhook drop it. A 4xx goes again
  too: a wrong token or address, fixed in the environment, gets through
  on the next attempt. A job keeps no address of its own: it goes to
  board.Webhook as main has it when the job goes
- AfterCommit stays where deletePost removes the files: short, and what
  a missed call leaves is a file, not a lost notice

TestNotify is TestDeliver now: one try of a job, its answer or none
within notifyWithin. TestDrafts runs the worker one step at a time,
outbox.RunOnce, at a time of its own, and sleeps not at all. With no
webhook, publishing writes no job. Then the webhook is down at first:
the job is taken, fails, and is not due again at once. It is up again:
at the job's RunAt, read from the database, the webhook hears of the
post, its id, key, title and path, under the same Idempotency-Key, and
the job is gone. The draft has a key of its own, so that the body's key
is checked.

Maago-Run: maago add outbox

